{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_16","type":"agent_message","text":"The profile exposed a tile-layout cliff: the initial 8×128 tile took about 0.194 ms at the largest shape, while a 4×256 tile performs the identical fused work in about 0.059 ms. That drops the estimated full call from ~0.409 ms to ~0.274 ms. A two-pass design and register-gather design were both slower, so I’m narrowing the remaining sweep around the 4×256 wave-aligned layout and checking whether size-dependent dispatch helps short sequences."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport torch, triton\nimport kernel\nh=2048\nmaxm=8192\nbcx=torch.randn((maxm,3*h),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16)\ncw=torch.randn((h,1,4),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16)\ncb=torch.randn((h,),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16)\ny=torch.empty((maxm,h),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16)\nconfigs=[(2,256,2),(2,256,4),(4,256,2),(4,256,4),(4,256,8),(2,512,4),(2,512,8),(4,512,8)]\nfor m in (256,1024,2048,4096,8192):\n  print('M',m)\n  for bm,bh,nw in configs:\n    try:\n      fn=lambda bm=bm,bh=bh,nw=nw,m=m: kernel._causal_gate_kernel[(triton.cdiv(m,bm),triton.cdiv(h,bh))](bcx,cw,cb,y,M=m,S=m,H=h,BLOCK_M=bm,BLOCK_H=bh,num_warps=nw)\n      print((bm,bh,nw),round(triton.testing.do_bench(fn,warmup=10,rep=30),6))\n    except Exception as e:\n      print((bm,bh,nw),'ERR',str(e).splitlines()[-1])\nprint('waves_per_eu M8192 tile 4x256')\nfor wpe in (1,2,3,4):\n  try:\n    fn=lambda wpe=wpe: kernel._causal_gate_kernel[(triton.cdiv(maxm,4),triton.cdiv(h,256))](bcx,cw,cb,y,M=maxm,S=maxm,H=h,BLOCK_M=4,BLOCK_H=256,num_warps=4,waves_per_eu=wpe)\n    print(wpe,triton.testing.do_bench(fn,warmup=10,rep=30))\n  except Exception as e:\n    print(wpe,'ERR',str(e).splitlines()[-1])\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
