{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_20","type":"agent_message","text":"At the verified 4×256 layout, the fused middle stage is no longer the bottleneck: on the largest case it is ~0.052 ms versus ~0.158 ms for the 3-way input projection and ~0.057 ms for the output projection. I’m testing a native Triton BF16 GEMM with fused bias against those library calls. I’ll only adopt it if it is both faster across the shape range and stays inside the workload’s matched-ratio rule."}}
