{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_23","type":"agent_message","text":"The library GEMMs are already decisively better than the tested native Triton tiles, so I’m keeping them. One remaining correctness detail is worth tightening before the final attempt: the current four-tap reduction runs newest-to-oldest, while the convolution library may accumulate oldest-to-newest and add bias last. I’m comparing those orderings directly at the BF16 convolution boundary; this can eliminate the rare outliers without changing speed."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"python - <<'PY'\nimport torch\nimport torch.nn.functional as F\n\ntorch.manual_seed(123)\nb,s,h=1,256,2048\nx=torch.randn((b,s,h),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16)\nw=torch.randn((3*h,h),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16)\nbias=torch.randn((3*h,),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16)\ncw=torch.randn((h,1,4),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16)\ncb=torch.randn((h,),device='cuda',dtype=torch.bfloat16)\nbcx=F.linear(x,w,bias).transpose(1,2)\nB,C,X=bcx.chunk(3,dim=1)\nbx=B*X\nref=F.conv1d(F.pad(bx,(3,0)),cw,cb,groups=h)\npad=F.pad(bx,(3,0))\nterms=[pad[:,:,k:k+s].float()*cw[:,0,k][None,:,None].float() for k in range(4)]\nvariants={}\nfor order_name,order in [('forward',range(4)),('reverse',range(3,-1,-1))]:\n  for bias_first in (False,True):\n    acc=cb[None,:,None].float().expand_as(terms[0]).clone() if bias_first else torch.zeros_like(terms[0])\n    for k in order: acc=acc+terms[k]\n    if not bias_first: acc=acc+cb[None,:,None].float()\n    got=acc.bfloat16()\n    neq=(got\"'!=ref)\n    variants[(order_name,bias_first)]=(neq.float().mean().item(),(got.float()-ref.float()).abs().max().item())\nprint(variants)\nPY'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
